BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holy Cross Wind Ensemble Concert: Nightfall
DTSTART:20261023T233000
DTEND:20261024T003000
DTSTAMP:20261024T150846Z
UID:f0440dec771e5e4ffee71d1757caa9@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:The Holy Cross Wind Ensemble presents Nightfall\, a concert in
 spired by the changing season and the transition from day into night. As O
 ctober gives us darker evenings\, the program takes listeners through autu
 mn landscapes\, shifting light\, and imaginations running wild. Autumn is 
 a season of change. The brilliant colors of fall in New England gradually 
 give way to bare branches and longer nights\, creating a landscape that is
  stark\, reflective\, and mysterious. The program begins in the warmth of 
 the season with works such as Julie Giroux's Bookmarks from Japan and Perc
 y Grainger's Irish Tune from County Derry. Eric Whitacre's October capture
 s the character of autumn itself\, evoking the feelings of the season thro
 ugh rich musical colors. As the evening unfolds\, the music moves toward t
 wilight\, mystery\, and darkness. Eric Whitacre's Ghost Train draws upon A
 merican folklore and the imagination that emerges after nightfall. Togethe
 r\, these works trace a path from daylight into night and from autumn towa
 rd winter\, exploring the beauty and mystery that accompany this seasonal 
 transition. Dress Code: Casual (jeans ok) --- Event Details: https://myhc.
 holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152344\n\nSource: College of the Holy Cross\nEvent 
 page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152344
LOCATION:Luth Concert Hall Prior Performing Arts Center\, 1 College Street
 \, Worcester\, MA 01610\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152344
END:VEVENT
