DTEND:20261107T150000
DTSTAMP:20261024T150847Z
UID:ad03466c485e07ce54f2e10bc09f6a@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Hold Me Tender\, Bayda Asbridge’s series of boat sculptures 
 on view 10/22-11/21 at the Mary Cosgrove Dolphin Gallery\, examines identi
 ty\, displacement\, and belonging. Using muted colors\, natural materials
 \, and woven textures\, the boats—some shrouded\, others suspended or fr
 actured—evoke both fragility and resilience. Join Bayda for this hands-o
 n workshop and construct your own boat sculpture while learning about the 
 artist’s motivation and process. Free and open to the public. No registr
 ation required\, just drop in!\n\nSource: Worcester State University\nEven
 t page: https://www.worcester.edu/event/create-your-own-boat-sculpture-wit
 h-artist-bayda-asbridge-2/
LOCATION:Mary Cosgrove Dolphin Gallery\, Ghosh Science and Technology Cent
 er
URL:https://www.worcester.edu/event/create-your-own-boat-sculpture-with-ar
 tist-bayda-asbridge-2/
END:VEVENT
