DESCRIPTION:November 10\, 2026\, 7:30 PM\, TFAC\, Curtis Performance Hall 
 John Hodgen is the recipient of numerous awards\, including the AWP’s Do
 nald Hall Prize for Poetry. He is the author of six collections of poetry
 \, including\, most recently\, What We May Be. Christie Hodgen’s awards 
 include two Pushcart Prizes\, a Guggenheim Fellowship\, a grant from the N
 ational Endowment for the Arts\, and AWP’s prize for the novel (for Boy 
 Meets Girl) and AWP’s prize for short fiction (for A Jeweler’s Eye for
  Flaw). She is also the author of Elegies for the Brokenhearted and Hello
 \, I Must Be Going.\n\nSource: Assumption University\nEvent page: https://
 www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/events/an-evening-of-poetry-and-fiction
 -with-john-hodgen-and-christie-hodgen-humanarts
LOCATION:Curtis Performance Hall\, Tsotsis Family Academic Center\, 500 Sa
 lisbury Street\, Worcester\, MA\, 01609
URL:https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/events/an-evening-of-poetry
 -and-fiction-with-john-hodgen-and-christie-hodgen-humanarts
